[Music]  family of Aretha Franklin continues to  plan memorial events following the  legendary soul singers death on Thursday  at the age of 76 her funeral will be  held at a four thousand seat Church in  her native Detroit just a few miles down  the road from the church that sewed the  Queens of Souls royal roots back in 2011  for CBS Sunday morning  I had a chance to go to that church with  Aretha  this is your spot this is where I sit  when I come to church this is where this  is my seat don't sit in my seat father  the charismatic Reverend CL Franklin who  was pastor he would Electrify audiences  with his thunderous sir  [Music]  then he called his daughter up to the  pulpit my dad had to push me the same  though I really didn't want to sing  Aretha was about ten years old I'm  standing up on a little box a box  yeah the pulpit was too high so they put  a little box next to the pulpit so this  was this was your place yeah this is  where we lived we went back to the  Franklin family home in West Detroit you  were saying in the day it was a  showplace yeah it was definitely a  showplace it was the most beautiful home  I had ever seen there was a room right  the second floor yeah right there when  gospel greats like Mahalia Jackson or  Clara ward would visit the house the  young Aretha would watch from the top of  the stairs see who was coming in and who  was going out and peopling through the  railing of the staircase so it was  special yeah very very special who did  you like to see most of all anytime  Aretha 's life was also marked by  tragedy her mother who moved away when  she was six died four years later in her  autobiography  Aretha wrote I cannot describe the pain  nor will I try in 1979 her father was  shot during a burglary in their Detroit  home he lingered in a coma for five  years before his death when we were  trying to get the car  Aretha asked the city to dedicate a  local park to him she wanted us to see  it  but as we approached the park she was  overcome by emotion that still means a  lot - it took a minute for her to  compose herself  it's beautiful park I'm glad they  dedicated it to you  Reverend Franklin envisioned a great  career for his talented daughter but  likely even he did not imagine she would  live to perform at the inauguration of  the first african-american president  [Music]  that goes down in history I'm thankful  that I was a part of that pretty amazing  life incur that she had and what an  extraordinary day that was I will I will  never forget that day was there one  standout mobile they were cut me and  obviously she got very emotional talking  about her father very unexpectedly when  we approached the park I remember that  and I will always remember her blushing  when she mentioned it was like she was  that 14 year old girl again at the top  of the stairs you know the only  beautiful thing in the last couple of  days has been all the songs that we've  gotten to hear over and over and over  and that's the thing and that's what  will survive it's one of the most  incredible catalogs I mean I think of  her as the greatest singer of our time  just an incredible voice an incredible  emotion such an original too and you  know that tableau of that ending shot  they're really just so symbolic so  powerful things Anthony

